---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import DocSection from '../components/DocSection.astro';
import HandoverPack from '../components/HandoverPack.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data';
import Flow from '../components/Flow.astro';
import { FileText, Globe, Monitor, Server, Gauge, Layers, Accessibility, BookOpen } from 'lucide-react';

// Re-measure and update these when the site changes (Lighthouse, mobile settings, production build).
const measuredOn = 'October 12, 2026';
const scores = [
	{ label: 'Performance', value: '98' },
	{ label: 'Accessibility', value: '100' },
	{ label: 'Best practices', value: '100' },
	{ label: 'SEO', value: '100' },
];
---

<Layout
	title={`How this site was built | ${SITE.name}`}
	description="The site itself as a case study: measured performance, accessibility and the documentation behind it."
>
	<Header />
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20 lg:px-8">
		<SectionHeading
			as="h1"
			id="built-heading"
			heading="How this site was built"
			copy={`The clearest evidence of how ${SITE.shortName} works is the site you're reading. Here is what went into it, with numbers you can check yourself.`}
		/>

		<Flow
			class="mt-12"
			steps={[
				{ icon: FileText, title: 'Built ahead', note: 'Every page is turned into plain HTML before anyone visits.' },
				{ icon: Globe, title: 'Served nearby', note: "Vercel's network sends it from a location close to you." },
				{ icon: Monitor, title: 'Your browser', note: 'About 122 KB per page, and almost no JavaScript to run.' },
				{ icon: Server, title: 'One function', note: 'The only server code: checking and sending the contact form.' },
			]}
			caption="This site's whole architecture, start to finish."
		/>

		<DocSection heading="Measured" icon={Gauge}>
			<dl class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-6 sm:grid-cols-4">
				{scores.map((s) => (
					<div class="border-t border-ink pt-3">
						<dt class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{s.label}</dt>
						<dd class="display mt-1 text-5xl text-ink">{s.value}</dd>
					</div>
				))}
			</dl>
			<p>
				Lighthouse scores for the homepage on Google's mobile settings (a mid-range phone on a slow 4G connection),
				measured {measuredOn}. Run the same test on any page with Chrome DevTools or{' '}
				<a href="https://pagespeed.web.dev" class="link" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
					PageSpeed Insights
				</a>
				.
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>About 122 KB</strong> to load the homepage, including both typefaces.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Under 1 KB of JavaScript</strong> on most pages; about 5 KB on the contact page, for form validation.
					No framework code is sent to the browser.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>No tracking cookies</strong>, so there is no consent banner to click through.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</DocSection>

		<DocSection heading="How it's put together" icon={Layers}>
			<ul>
				<li>Every page is pre-built static HTML (Astro), so there is nothing to compute when you visit.</li>
				<li>
					The only server code is the contact form: one small function that validates your message and sends it by
					email.
				</li>
				<li>Interface components from shadcn/ui, rendered to plain HTML ahead of time rather than in your browser.</li>
				<li>Two typefaces, hosted with the site instead of loaded from a third party.</li>
			</ul>
		</DocSection>

		<DocSection heading="Accessibility" icon={Accessibility}>
			<p>
				Headings in order on every page, a label on every form field, visible keyboard focus, error messages tied to the
				field they describe, colour contrast at WCAG AA, and reduced motion respected.{' '}
				<a href="/accessibility" class="link">
					Read the accessibility statement
				</a>
				.
			</p>
		</DocSection>

		<DocSection heading="Documentation" icon={BookOpen}>
			<p>
				A handover includes the documentation, not just the code. This site's repository has the same set a client
				project would:
			</p>
			<HandoverPack
				folder="plumbline-web/"
				tag="This site"
				files={[
					{ name: 'README.md', note: 'How to run it locally, configure email and deploy' },
					{ name: 'PRODUCT_SPEC.md', note: 'What it must do, with every change as a dated revision' },
					{ name: 'DESIGN.md', note: 'Colours, type, spacing and components, written down' },
					{ name: 'src/data.ts', note: 'All shared content in one place, so edits stay consistent' },
					{ name: 'vercel.json', note: 'Security and caching headers, in version control' },
					{ name: '.env.example', note: 'Every setting the site needs, none of the secrets' },
				]}
				caption="The real documentation set behind this site; a client project gets the same."
			/>
		</DocSection>
	</main>
	<ContactCTA heading="Want software built like this?" copy="Tell us what you're trying to build, improve, or solve." />
	<Footer />
</Layout>
